FOR THESE REASONS, THE COURT,

Decides, unanimously, to join to the merits the Government’s objections regarding the applicant’s victim status and dismisses it;

Declares, unanimously, the application admissible under Article 3 of the Convention;

Holds, unanimously, that there has been a violation of the respondent State’s positive obligations under Article 3 of the Convention;

Holds, by five votes to two, that in the absence of a quantified claim, there is no legal basis for an award of just satisfaction.

